<title>GERMANY: Pan-German Aug industry output up 0.8 pct m/m.</title>
<headline>Pan-German Aug industry output up 0.8 pct m/m.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The economics ministry reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> PAN-GERMAN INDUSTRY OUTPUT  Aug 96    July 96     Aug 95</p>
<p> Month-on-month change(pct)   +0.8	 +1.1	 -1.5</p>
<p> Year-on-year		     +1.8	 -0.5	 n/a</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)	     100.3	 99.5	 98.5</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are seasonally adjusted and provisional. The year-on-year figures are calculated by Reuters from Bundesbank statistics.</p>
<p>The ministry gave the following details:</p>
<p>				    Aug 96		  July 96</p>
<p>				Index   Pct change  Index   Pct change</p>
<p> Mining			73.9	-0.8	74.5	-2.6</p>
<p> Manufacturing output    99.1	+1.7	97.4	+0.7</p>
<p> Incl:Intermed. goods   103.3	+2.6     100.7	+1.1</p>
<p> 1Capital goods	    96.7	+0.5	96.2	+0.7</p>
<p>	Consumer durables  92.4	+4.9	88.1	+1.5</p>
<p>	Consumer goods     96.9	+0.3	96.6	-1.1</p>
<p> Energy output	    108.4	+1.8     106.5	-0.1</p>
<p> Construction	     113.1	-6.1     120.4	+5.3</p>
<p>Two month comparison July/Aug 96 with May/June 96:</p>
<p> Industrial output		     +2.0</p>
<p> Manufacturing output		  +2.0</p>
<p> Construction			    +1.0</p>
<p> Capital goods			   +1.5</p>
<p> Mining				    -4.0</p>
<p> Energy output			   +1.0</p>
<p> Consumer durables		     +5.5</p>
<p> Consumer goods			  -2.0</p>
<p> Intermediate goods		    +3.0</p>
<p>Two month comparison July/Aug 1996 with July/Aug 1995:</p>
<p> Industrial output			+0.9</p>
<p> Mining				     -7.6</p>
<p> Manufacturing output:		  +2.4</p>
<p>  Incl: Intermediate goods	    +1.4</p>
<p>	  Capital goods		   +3.5</p>
<p>	  Consumer durables	     +9.0</p>
<p>	  Consumer goods		  -0.4</p>
<p> Energy output			    +5.3</p>
<p> Construction			     -7.1</p>
<p>-- William Boston, Bonn newsroom, 49-228-2609750</p>
</text>
